<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10427" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">con-scindo</span></b> , ĭdi, issum,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a.,
				to tear</i> or <i>rend to pieces</i> (very rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Lit: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pallulam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Truc. 1, 1, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 5, 1, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">epistulam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 7, 18, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ipsam capillo for illius capillum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Eun. 4, 3, 4</span></i>
			 Ruhnk.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quā dominus, quā advocati
					sibilis conscissi,</span>”
				<i>hissed at</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 2, 19, 3</span></i>
			; cf.: is me ab optimatibus ait conscindi, <i>am
				pulled to pieces</i>, i. e. <i>abused,
			calumniated</i>, <i><span class="en">id. ib. 8, 16,
		1</span></i>.</div>
